  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With an integer `n`, output **any** array containing `n` **unique** integers such that they add up to `0`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 5\nOutput: [-7,-1,1,3,4]\nExplanation: These arrays also are accepted [-5,-1,1,2,3] , [-3,-1,2,-2,4].\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: [-1,0,1]\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 1\nOutput: [0]\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
